WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.560
The people of Old Yharnam were dying.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.420
They called it "ashen blood"; a baffling
sickness that ravaged the town.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.429
It's not hard to imagine what the
symptoms were. And the only treatment they

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:12.960
had

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.660
were these little white tablets, and even
these only offered temporary relief.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:22.890
There weren't a cure, not by a long shot. So
when the Healing Church appeared

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.160
proclaiming salvation via their blood
transfusions

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.820
it probably came at the perfect time. The
people were cured

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.340
of their "ashen blood ailment" and the
Church's miracle cure

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.980
became the pride of Yharnam and the
envy of outsiders.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.190
People would come from far and wide for a chance

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.610
at blood ministration, and the Healing
Church gained unprecedented power

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.289
through the faith of its people.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:50.300
Only, don't you think this is all too
convenient?

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.059
That there would be a sickness of the
blood? That it would only affect the

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:55.539
populace of Old Yharnam?

00:00:55.539 --> 00:00:59.940
That the Healing Church was ready and
waiting with transfusions that could

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.019
cure anything?

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:05.770
No. It's possible the Healing Church
poisoned the populace of Old Yharnam

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.420
with the ashen blood ailment. The "Poison
Knife" tells us that "poison was a weapon

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.259
of the Church",

00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:14.409
the antidote tablets, that the populace
used to treat

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:17.509
ashen blood, cure poison, and

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:22.130
underneath Old Yharnam runs a water supply
that could have been easily tainted.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.759
What better way to create a community
ready to accept

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:30.500
the miracles the Healing Church? But,
regardless of what you believe,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.409
it's a fact that the ashen blood
ailment eventually triggered the spread

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:38.990
"the beastly scourge". And since Old Yharnam was one of the first places treated with

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:39.810
the old blood,

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.899
its people were among the first to turn.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.539
"The Hunter's Workshop" existed to fight

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:49.860
the scourge of beasts. It was one branch of
the Church

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.530
run by Gehrman, The First Hunter. The
hunters workshop itself consisted of

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:57.670
factions each with different ideas on
beast hunting.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:01.460
One of these factions were the "Powder Keg
Hunters, Bearers

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.780
of the Powder Keg Badge." The Powder Keg
Hunters

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.590
are credited with creations such as the
"Cannon", the "Rifle Spear",

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.130
the "Stake Driver", and perhaps even
molotov cocktails,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:15.950
but these are unlocked when you attain
their badge. The late Powder Kegs had a

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:16.549
motto,

00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:21.420
"If a weapon ain't got kick, it just ain't worth it".
They were labeled heretics

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.859
by the rest of the Workshop who spurned
their crude genius.

00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:29.079
But you can't deny they had character. One of the Powder Keg Hunters

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:30.340
was Djura.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.620
He was said to have been uncommonly kind,
and dreadfully

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.620
foolish; and he wasn't just any hunter,

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.349
he was a hunter of the dream. The hunter's
dream sustained him,

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:44.390
allowing him to suffer little
consequence from death, enabling him

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.870
to venture out into the waking world
from the safety of another realm.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.269
Who knows for how long he did this, and
for what reasons.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:55.970
Perhaps he saw a great good in what the
workshop was doing,

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:59.560
their hunting of beasts kept the populace
safe. Though

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.060
it can't have been too long before
everything got out of hand.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.319
A couple of people turning into beasts
was manageable,

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:11.160
but when the Blood Moon descended, the
line between man and beast was blurred.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.069
And "Old Yharnam", one of the first
places treated with the "old blood",

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:19.610
became severely overrun by beasts. At
this point

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.459
secrecy was impossible, and no longer
required. The

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:27.579
only way to contain the beasts was
to launch an all-out assault on Old Yharnam.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:30.980
And who better for the job than the Powder
Keg Hunters?

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.639
Old Yharnam was sealed and set
ablaze

00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:38.410
to prevent the spread of the beastly
scourge. The town burned,

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:42.030
and so did the men, women, children, and
beasts within it.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.630
We find the "Charred Hunter Set" within the
ruins;

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:49.250
worn by the hunters who swept through
after the raging flames

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.709
subsided, to hunt victims of the scourge who survived the inferno.

00:03:53.709 --> 00:03:56.819
It vividly mentions the stench of
singed

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:01.620
blood. The weaponry, attire, and over enthusiasm 
of the Powder Kegs

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.030
was clearly visible in the smoking
debris that remained.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.650
There is little doubt that they were
responsible, but

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:12.420
the Hunters did not perform this purge 
eagerly. In fact,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.760
we see a certain reluctance in the notes
left behind.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.539
"The red moon hangs low, and beasts rule
the streets.

00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:23.190
Are we left no other choice, than to burn it
all to cinders?"

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.180
Time passes and "Central Yharnam" becomes
the heart of the city,

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.760
and Old Yharnam becomes this
distant memory that lies

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.200
smoldering and forgotten. But when we
venture down

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.720
into the ruins of Old Yharnam, we
find that one human

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.820
still remains within,

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.580
Djura. "You there, Hunter.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.389
Didn't you see the warning?

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:51.789
Turn back at once. Old Yharnam

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:57.139
burned and abandoned by men, is now home only to beasts.

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:02.709
They are of no harm to those above. Turn back, or the hunter

00:05:02.709 --> 00:05:08.819
will face the hunt." Djura felt defeated by the state of Old Yharnam.

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:13.149
So much so that he renounced his Hunter's
vows and pledged never to kill another

00:05:13.149 --> 00:05:13.909
beast.

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:18.839
This kind, foolish man found his true
calling in protecting the beasts of

00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:19.489
Yharnam

00:05:19.489 --> 00:05:22.599
from the hunter he used to be. "You

00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:25.700
are a skilled hunter. Adept,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.850
merciless, half-cut with blood. As the best hunters

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.090
are. Which is

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:39.860
why I must stop you!"

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.069
"I should think you still have dreams?

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:46.640
Well, the next time you dream,

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:52.870
give some thought to the hunt..." No one truly knows the hunts purpose.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.220
It is watched over by a man who does not wish to be there,

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:59.900
and it's inhabited by a doll who exists
to serve you.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.220
There is no explanation for why we
venture out

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:08.370
and kill. For Djura, Old Yharnam was his
realization that hunters are no better

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.030
than the beasts that they've slain,

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:14.290
and it's true really. If a beast is
characterized by

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:18.030
its mindless thirst for blood, then are
hunters really

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.500
any different? Some beasts are even
capable

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.990
speech and of reason. "Die! Die! Hunters are

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.100
killers, nothing less!

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.120
You call ME a beast? A Beast!?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.810
What would you know? I didn't ask for this!"

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:40.580
"You hunters have got more blood on your hands."

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:46.490
"I no longer dream, but I was once a hunter too.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:50.170
There's nothing more horrific than a hunt.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:55.200
In case you fail to realize, the
things you hunt,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.180
they're not beasts, they're people.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.860
You're not hunting beasts;

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:06.730
it's you, you're the beast.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.160
Just think about what you're doing.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.320
It's utter madness.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.880
One day you will see."

